    "history": {
      "value": "Headline began in 1997 in Santa Barbara as Bertelsmann Ventures, an internet fund led by Jan Henric Buettner and Wolfgang Rose, and became BV Capital in 2000 with Mathias Schilling and Thomas Gieselmann, then e.ventures in 2012 and Headline in 2021. It became known for bets on Sonos, Farfetch, Bumble and Mistral AI. Today it runs early stage funds for the US and Europe and a global growth fund, the latest of which closed at $865 million in 2024.",
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Headline_(company)",
      "basis": "Founding and names: Wikipedia 'Headline (company)' (Bertelsmann Ventures 1997 in Santa Barbara, founded by Jan Henric Buettner and Wolfgang Rose; BV Capital 2000 with Buettner, Rose, Mathias Schilling and Thomas Gieselmann; e.ventures 2012; Headline 2021) and TechCrunch 2012-07-15 on the e.ventures rename. Bets: Sonos (BV Capital, 2005), Farfetch, Bumble (growth fund, 2020), Mistral AI (seed, 2023), all members of the portfolio on this page. Latest fund: Headline Global Growth IV at $865M (Fortune 2024-09-18, https://fortune.com/2024/09/18/headline-raises-865-million-hires-new-head-of-growth/). Moved to this sidecar to fit the shape rule: the move from Santa Barbara to San Francisco; offices in Berlin, Hamburg, Paris and London; the Asia desk (Infinity Ventures, now Headline Asia, own fund family, out of the portfolio on this page, decisions.md D2) and the Brazil desk (Redpoint eventures, later Headline Brazil, out, D3); US VII $408M and EU VII EUR 320M (TechCrunch 2022-07-07); the firm's early check of $1.5M to $15M."
    },
    "investment_concept": {
      "value": "“Global venture capital helping founders win, bigger.”",
      "source": "https://headline.com/",
      "basis": "The firm's own line, read 2026-09-27: the homepage carries no headline element (a rotating highlights strip opens with 'Over 25 years, it's been our honor to work alongside exceptional founders.'), so the title-tag tagline stands: 'Headline | Global Venture Capital Helping Founders Win, Bigger', set in sentence case with one closing period. Competing lines on the same page: the section title 'A boutique firm with global wingspan.'; the meta description 'Headline is a global venture capital firm with teams across the US, Europe, Asia, and Brazil. ...'; the footer 'Headline is a venture capital firm with dedicated teams on the ground around the world.' Published inside quotation marks, as the firm's own words (Erik, 2026-09-26)."
    },
    "investment_stage": {
